    {
      "id": "amN2Qdtz4DvoQy8kk-z3a",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -30.678999066352844,
      "y": 1733.4828871091204,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "Eh4nyBAK3NijA3kGgBf0Q"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1232032363,
      "version": 1054,
      "versionNonce": 1722656875,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788610056993,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Consider a concrete deployment where you want to serve a 13B LLM (e.g. Meta’s Llama 2 13B) on AWS.\n\nAWS’s g5.2xlarge instance has one NVIDIA A10G GPU with 24 GB of VRAM. AWS has published an on-\ndemand example price of $1.212/hour.\n\n                                          1.212 × 24 × 30 = $872.64/month\n\nOur model in full precision (FP32) need approximately:\n\n                                                  13B × 4bytes = 52 GB\n\nBut our GPU has only 24 GB :(\n\nSo we quantize to a lower precision (FP32 → INT8) so that each parameter requires less bytes.\n\nLet's say we quantize so that each parameter now need 1byte:\n\n                                                   13B × 1bytes = 13 GB\n\nNow the model can realistically fit.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Consider a concrete deployment where you want to serve a 13B LLM (e.g. Meta’s Llama 2 13B) on AWS.\n\nAWS’s g5.2xlarge instance has one NVIDIA A10G GPU with 24 GB of VRAM. AWS has published an on-demand example price of $1.212/hour.\n\n                                          1.212 × 24 × 30 = $872.64/month\n\nOur model in full precision (FP32) need approximately:\n\n                                                  13B × 4bytes = 52 GB\n\nBut our GPU has only 24 GB :(\n\nSo we quantize to a lower precision (FP32 → INT8) so that each parameter requires less bytes.\n\nLet's say we quantize so that each parameter now need 1byte:\n\n                                                   13B × 1bytes = 13 GB\n\nNow the model can realistically fit.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1xwIXIKcCiRFq_nMaxBCl",
