      "updated": 1788800653797,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Static post-training quantization\n- new levels of qualitaziones: 8, 4, but also 3 and 2 (weight-only)\n- the core tecnological advancement is row-wise quantization (per-channel) and modified Optimal Brain\nQuantization\n- 4bit vs FP16: 4x memory savings, some inference speed and negligeble perf degradation ???????(look at\nthe benchmarkls)\n- for quantization time take 4GPU/h to quantize BLOOM176B\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Static post-training quantization\n- new levels of qualitaziones: 8, 4, but also 3 and 2 (weight-only)\n- the core tecnological advancement is row-wise quantization (per-channel) and modified Optimal Brain Quantization\n- 4bit vs FP16: 4x memory savings, some inference speed and negligeble perf degradation ???????(look at the benchmarkls)\n- for quantization time take 4GPU/h to quantize BLOOM176B\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
